{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310548,"nonce":"4ryYhKY5pVZTl/yMz9GY/4oPGCk=","title":"c_backend silently no-ops MarkMoved/CheckLive. This is correct (strict enforcement happens in the HIR/TAST layer via E0300 before backend ...","message":"`compiler/src/codegen/c_backend.rs:642-644` (and similarly `mir_interpreter.rs` when `RAYZOR_STRICT_MOVE_CHECK` is off) silently no-ops the `MarkMoved` / `CheckLive` arms.\n\n**Why this is correct today:** strict `@:move` enforcement happens at compile time via E0300/E0382 hard errors in the use-after-move diagnostic pass over TAST. By the time MIR reaches a backend, any use-after-move that the static analyser caught has already prevented the program from compiling. The runtime CheckLive trap path on Cranelift is a belt-and-braces guard for cases the static analyser misses (e.g. dynamic dispatch through closures).\n\n**Why this is misleading:** a contributor reading `c_backend.rs:642-644` sees two opcodes with empty bodies and a one-line comment. They could reasonably conclude that the C backend is exempt from move-checking, or that move-checking is a Cranelift-only feature.\n\n**How to apply:** add a comment block above the C backend arms explaining the layering — strict-move E0300 fires at TAST → HIR transition before any backend codegen runs; the runtime CheckLive trap is a Cranelift-specific belt-and-braces guard for dynamic-dispatch escape cases the static analyser cannot prove. C backend has no equivalent trap because cc compiles AOT and panics would be invisible to JIT debuggers.\n\nBundle with the next c_backend.rs touch; don't ship as a standalone doc commit.\n\nRelated: [[project-move-clone-enforced]], [[bugs-cranelift-liveness-dead-params]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_c_backend_move_noop` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}